coverage.out

# Load-test credentials. sessions.json holds bearer tokens for the tenants cmd/loadseed created;
# they expire with AccessTokenTTL and are regenerated by `make load-seed`.
load/sessions.json

# results.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the machine-readable record behind the numbers
# quoted in the README, and it is committed for the same reason the ADRs are: a figure whose
# evidence lives only on the machine that produced it is a claim rather than a measurement.
# handleSummary deletes the sessions from it before writing, so the committed artifact carries no
# credentials — and that deletion happened because the pre-fix run embedded all thirty tokens.
